{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 57, :comments ["<b>And these are the numbered of the Levites</b> – I do not know why He counts the Levites, and what benefit there is now in their counting. Perhaps it is to these that the cities were given for dwelling and their open lands for their livestock, not to those born afterward. Or it was done for them as an honor before HaShem, so that the legion of the King should not be lesser, that they would not attend to count it as the rest of the people. And He mentioned Amram and his wife because the Levites are counted in two ways, for priests and for Levites, and it is fitting to count Aaron and his sons by themselves:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "Reading לא יהיה לגיון של מלך פחות, 'so that the legion of the King should not be lesser,' as the plain sense of the difficult phrase."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:00.463443066Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}